  "query_preview": "..A quick discussion today as active weather\ncontinues. Looking at the latest mesoanalysis, SBCAPE continues to\nclimb to near 1000-1500 J/kg. With little deep layer shear, storm\nmotions have been very slow. The biggest question in regard to any\nflash flood threat will be whether storms are able to sustain\nshear/cold pool balance and continue to shift with outflow\nboundaries. This will be something to monitor over the next few\nhours.  \n\nExcessive Heat Warnings and Heat Advisories continue for many\nlocations. For southern Utah, these continue through Saturday, the\nremainder of Utah through Sunday. No changes were made with this\npackage to the heat headlines.\n\nLooking at the latest runs of the HRRR, CAMs may be trending\ntoward more convective coverage Saturday. SBCAPE values will be\nslightly less than today, with little to no deep layer shear. Cold\npool/shear balance will be a question again. \n\nThis monsoon surge will continue to spread north and east Sunday\ninto Monday and continue through much of the week. Storm motions\nand shear will increase to an extent Sunday into early next week,\nwhich may allow for more intense rainfall rates.",
